  "evidence": "TEXT_G: 31% flat tax merging income tax and NI; workfare for some claimants and restricting benefits to citizens/residents of five years; retain/expand grammar and specialist schools with broader merit assessments; five‑year freeze on settlement and long‑term immigration cap (~50,000 p.a.), no amnesty, restore Primary Purpose Rule, tripled border staffing; withdraw from the EU, reaffirm primacy of UK law, end government promotion of multiculturalism, English‑only sittings, Commonwealth Day; large defence build‑up (+~40%), maintain/replace nuclear deterrent; law and order focus with “life means life”, double prison capacity, end early release, “three strikes”, stronger self‑defence rights, elected police boards; repeal the Human Rights Act and withdraw from the ECHR.\nTEXT_D: Equality/care measures including a £2.5bn Pupil Premium, phased abolition of tuition fees, pay audits and name‑blind applications, strengthened disability employment support, integrate health and social care with carers’ respite, fair energy/social tariffs, triple‑lock state pension; justice shift toward rehabilitation (presumption against <6‑month sentences, cancel new prison build, expand restorative justice); immigration/asylum liberalisation (earned citizenship for long‑term residents, end child detention, right to work for asylum seekers); civil‑liberties protections (retain Human Rights Act, scrap ID cards, curb surveillance); progressive tax changes (align CGT with income tax, 1% levy on property >£2m).",
